five funerals were held on thursday in  one of the deadliest days in the  occupied west bank in recent months  the palestinian victims were all killed  during confrontations with israeli  forces  this funeral is for 20 year old omar  alayan from silhad village near ramallah  paramedics told us the israeli army  delayed ambulances and assaulted them  before finally allowing them to reach  lyan 20 minutes after he was shot by  then  it was too late to save him  my son's only wish was to die for what  he believed in just like his whole  generation because they see no future  nor a political horizon for them  the palestinian red crescent says since  the beginning of this month medical  teams have been blocked from aiding the  wounded in five different incidents  in the past two weeks three attacks on  medical staff and another on an  ambulance were reported  two of those killed on thursday were  from jeanine north of the west bank  janine has become the center of the  current wave of escalation with almost  daily raids by israeli forces  hundreds of gunmen live in the janine  refugee camp and often return israeli  fire with fire  youth and ramallah are raging i'm not  only talking about me i know how every  young man is feeling the youth in  ramallah are all ready for escalation we  can't accept to just sit and watch our  brothers in genin and nablus and other  areas while they're resisting and being  killed and injured  the israeli military says it's  conducting a counter-terrorism operation  it started early april after two gunmen  from the jeanine area committed two  attacks in israel leaving eight israelis  dead palestinian prisoners groups say  israeli forces have arrested more than  200 palestinians since the operation  started but tensions stretch back longer  than that  since the beginning of the year more  than 1500 palestinians have been  detained and at least 41 palestinians  have been killed the majority in  confrontations with the israeli military  we're not just talking about the latest  attacks in israel as a starting point  for the current escalation yes indeed it  has contributed to heightened tensions  all across the west bank but  palestinians want the world to know that  they have been under occupation for  decades and it's rarely been a night in  the west bank where they haven't seen  the israeli army raid their cities  arrest people and sometimes shoot and  kill them  on thursday a general strike was  announced in three cities in the west  bank ramallah bethlehem and jeanine to  mourn the dead  palestinians fear that there will be  more israeli raids in the days ahead  ibrahim al-jazeera the occupied west  bank
 

